    "ls|LS17_S8_U_255": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF EDUCATION \nDEPARTMENT OF SCHOOL EDUCATION & LITERACY \n \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 255 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 21ST March, 2022 \n \nDropout from Schools under Delhi Government \n \n255. SHRI PARVESH SAHIB SINGH VERMA \n \nWill the Minister of EDUCATION be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the Government is aware of the number of schools under the ambit of the Delhi \nGovernment and the number of students enrolled in the current year and if so, the details \nthereof;  \n \n(b) whether the Government is also aware of the high number of dropouts from Delhi \nGovernment schools from class 9 onwards and if so, the details thereof;  \n \n(c) whether the Government has conducted any investigation to look into the reasons for the \nincreasing number o f students being pushed by the Delhi Government schools into National \nInstitute of Open Schooling centres over the years and if so, the details thereof; and  \n \n(d) Whether the Union Government proposes to hold talks with the Delhi Government to \nensure vulnerable students are not left out of the education fold? \n \nA N S W E R \nMINISTER OF EDUCATION \n(SHRI DHARMENDRA PRADHAN) \n \n(a) to (d):  A Statement is laid on the Table of the House.   \n\n \nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO (d) OF LOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO.255 TO BE ANSWERED ON 21 ST MARCH, 2022 ASKED \nBY SHRI PARVESH SAHIB SINGH VERMA REGARDING DROPOUT FROM \nSCHOOLS UNDER DELHI GOVERNMENT  \n \n(a): The Department of School Education and Literacy (DoSEL), Ministry of Education has \ndeveloped the Unifie d District Information System for Education Plus (UDISE+) system to \nrecord data on indicators of school education provided by all the States and Union Territories. \nAs per latest information based on UDISE 2019 -20, t he number of schools and students \nenrolled in them in case of Delhi, in the year 2019-20 is as under: \nManagement Schools Enrolment \nGovernment 2,767 23,09,819 \nOverall 5,679 41,80,617 \n \n(b):   The grade-wise annual average dropout  rate of Delhi Government schools from class 9 \nonwards based on UDISE 2019-20 is as under: \nGrade Wise Annual Average Dropout Rate – Delhi for 2019-20 \nYear Class - 9 Class -10 Class -11 \n2019-20 17.9 8.2 8.2 \n \n(c): The students of some categories, of Delhi Government Schools are being enrolled in \nNIOS, like the Students of class IX/X who were enrolled and had appeared in Annual Exam \nbut their result was declared as failed (one or more times)/ Compartment in the session , \nStudents of class IX/X who were enrolled and could n ot appear in annual exam in the session \nand whose School Leaving Certificate (SLC) must not have been issued etc. \n \n (d): Education is in the concurrent list of the Constitution and majority of the schools are \nunder the domain of the respective State and UT Government which is the appropriate \ngovernment under the RTE Act, 2009. Ministry of Education issues various advisories/  \nguidelines to all the States/UTs to ensure the implementation of all the provisions of the RTE \nAct, 2009 in their respective jurisdiction from time to time. Further half yearly meeting is \nconducted with State/UTs to monitor the progress of implementation of Samagra Shiksha \nprogram.  \n \nProject Approval Board (PAB) meeting is conducted every year with the respective State/UT \nGovernment to consider, discuss and approve the various interventions under the schemes \nprepared by the States and UTs based on their re quirements and priority areas under various \nschemes including the interventions aimed at ensuring that the students from disadvantaged \ngroups are brought into the education fold.   \n***  ",
    "ls|LS17_S8_U_256": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF EDUCATION \nDEPARTMENT OF HIGHER EDUCATION \n \nLOK SABHA \n \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 256 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 21.03.2022 \n \nResults of UGC-NET Exam \n \n256. SHRI RAJMOHAN UNNITHAN: \n \nWill the Minister of EDUCATION be pleased to state: \n \n(a)   whether the passing percentage of eligible candidates is 6 per cent for \n the two term examinations held in December, 2020 and June, 2021 as \n per the National Testing Agency (NTA) notification and if so, the details \n thereof; \n \n(b)  the current policy of the G overnment/NTA about the percentage of \n candidates clearing the University Grants Commission (UGC) -National \n Eligibility Test (NET) exams; \n \n(c) whether UGC -NET exam results of NTA for the two terms i.e. \n December, 2020 and June, 2021 were declared together recently; \n \n(d) whether the passing percentage would have increased to 12 per cent \n for UGC -NET eligibility as two term examinations were conducted \n together; and \n \n(e) if so, the details thereof and if not, the reasons therefor? \n \n \nANSWER \n \n \nMINISTER OF EDUCATION \n \n(SH. DHARMENDRA PRADHAN) \n \n \n(a) to (e) : A statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n \n \n \n \n\n \nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (A) TO ( E) OF LOK \nSABHA STARRED QUESTION NO.  256 TO BE ANSWERED ON \n21.03.2022 REGARDING “ RESULTS OF UGC -NET EXAM ” RAISE D BY \nSHRI RAJMOHAN UNNITHAN, HON’BLE MEMBER OF PARLIAMENT \n \n(a) to (c): Yes, Sir. As per policy decision of University Grants Commission \n(UGC) and criteria notified in the Information Bulletin of UGC -NET, 6% of \nappeared candidates in both the papers of UGC-NET were declared qualified \nfor December 2020 and June 2021 Cycles /terms together by National \nTesting Agency (NTA). \n(d) & (e): No. As per procedure and criteria for declaration of result, 6% of \nthe appeared candidates in both the papers are declared quali fied in each \nUGC-NET.   The online applications were invited for December 2020 Cycle \nUGC-NET in the month of February, 2021.   As a result of COVID-19 \npandemic, the said examination could not be conducted as per schedule.   \nSince June 2021 Cycle of UGC-NET w as also to be conducted, it was \ndecided to conduct the exam for both these cycles together. Hence, once \nagain the portal for inviting online applications for June, 2021 Cycle was \nopened in the month of August, 2021. The exam for both these cycles was \nconducted together and as per the criteria, 6% of appeared candidates of \nboth these cycles were declared qualified. \nThe qualifying criteria of UGC -NET being very scientific, the number of \nqualifying candidates increases automatically if the number of appearing \ncandidates increases. \n \n***** \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n ",
    "ls|LS17_S8_U_257": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF FINANCE \nDEPARTMENT OF REVENUE \n***** \n \nLOK SABHA \n \nSTARRED QUESTION NO.*257 \n \n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON MONDAY THE 21ST MARCH, 2022 \n                                                PHALGUNA  30, 1943 (SAKA)  \n \nIMPORT DUTY ON COTTON \n \n*257. SHRI KANUMURU RAGHU RAMA KRISHNA RAJU: \n \nWill the Minister of FINANCE be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the Government has received any proposal explaining the need for \nremoval of 10 per cent import duty on cotton to improve the Textiles and Clothing \nsector because of rising raw cotton and yarn prices;  \n \n(b) if so, the details thereof; and  \n \n(c) the measures being taken in this regard? \n \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTRY OF FINANCE \n(MS. NIRMALA SITHARAMAN) \n \n(a), (b) and (c): A statement is placed on the Table of the House. \n \n \n***** \n  \n\nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO THE LOK SABHA STARRED \nQUESTION NO.*257 RAISED BY SHRI KANUMURU RAGHU RAMA KRISHNA \nRAJU FOR 21ST MARCH, 2022 ON “IMPORT DUTY ON COTTON” \n \n(a & b)  Certain representations have been received requesting for removal of 5% Basic \nCustoms Duty (BCD), 5% Agriculture Infrastructure and Development Cess (AIDC) and 1%  \nSocial Welfare Surcharge (SWS) [10% of (BCD+AIDC)] on Raw Cotton.   \n \n(c)  The decision to impose 5% B asic Customs Duty, and, 5% Agriculture \nInfrastructure and Development Cess on imports of Raw Cotton in Union Budget 2021-22 has \nbeen taken to benefit domestic cotto n farmers. Imports of cotton had  surged significantly in \nlast few years, even though India is the largest producer of cotton in the world. All varieties of \ncotton, including those which were produced in India were being imported in large quantities. \nThis has impacted the Indian farmer adversely. Garment exporters would no t be affected as \nexporters have the option of  availing of benefit of schemes like advance authorization, duty \ndrawback, EoU, SEZ etc. Further, RoSCTL scheme for garment and made -ups has also been \nextended till March 2024. Further incentives under various schemes are also being provided to \nGarment sector. \n  \n \n***** \n \n \n ",
    "ls|LS17_S8_U_258": "����������������������������������������\n������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n��\n��������������������\n����������������������������������������������������\n����������������������������������������������������������\n��\n����������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n��\n����������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n��\n����������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n��������������\n��\n������ ������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n����������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n��������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n������ �������� ������������ �������������� ������������������ ���������������� ������ ���������������� �������������������������� ���������������������������� ������ ������������ ������������\n����������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n������ ������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n����������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n������ ����������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n������������������������������������������������