    "ls|LS17_S8_U_364": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF PANCHAYATI RAJ \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 364 \nANSWERED ON 29.03.2022 \n \nSTRENGTHENING OF PANCHAYATI RAJ SYSTEM \n \n \n*364 MS. RAMYA HARIDAS \n \nWill the Minister of PANCHAYATI RAJ be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the Government is working on a new action plan related to rural development through \nPanchayati Raj in the country and if so, the details thereof; \n(b) whether any proposal regarding further strengthening of Panchayati Raj system sent by some \nState Governments is pending with the Union Government; and \n(c) if so, the details thereof and the action taken by the Union Government thereon? \n \nANSWER \n \nTHE MINISTER OF PANCHAYATI RAJ \n \n(SHRI GIRIRAJ SINGH) \n \n(a) to (c): A statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n \n \n \n \n \n  \n\nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) to (c) OF THE LOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 364 FOR ANSWER ON 29.03.2022 REGARDING \nSTRENGTHENING OF PANCHAYATI RAJ SYSTEM \n \n \n(a) The Ministry of Panchayati Raj is working to actively involve the Panchayati Raj Institutions (PRIs) \nfor attainment of United Nation’s set targets of Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs) to ensure \npoverty free and enhanced livelihood, healthy, child friendly, water sufficient, clean and green, \nself-sufficient infrastructure, socially secured, good governed and gender parity villages by the \nyear 2030.   \n \n (b) No, Sir. \n \n(c) Does not arise. \n \n*** ",
    "ls|LS17_S8_U_365": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF HOUSING AND URBAN AFFAIRS \nLOK SABHA \n \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.  365 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON FEBRUARY 03, 2022 \nTARGETS UNDER SWACHH BHARAT MISSION-URBAN \n \nNO. \n 365.   SHRIMATI RATHVA GITABEN VAJESINGBHAI: \n \nWill the Minister of State for HOUSING AND URBAN AF FAIRS be \npleased to state: \n   \n(a)  the in-depth details of the Open Defecation Fr ee (ODF) Urban \nLocal Bodies (ULBs) in the country;  \n \n(b) whether the Government has recognized priority districts of \nGujarat or at the national level to achieve cent-pe rcent target \nand if so, the details thereof; \n \n(c) the details of cities declared ODF+ and ODF++ i n the country \nincluding the State of Gujarat; \n \n(d) whether the Government has data of target achie ved by the \nGovernment under Swachh Bharat Mission-Urban, if so , the \ndetails thereof and if not, the reasons therefor; and \n \n(e) whether the Government is facing any problems w hile \nconstructing toilets in ULBs and if so, the reasons  therefor and \nthe steps taken by the Government in this regard? \n \n \nANSWER \n \nTHE MINISTER OF  HOUSING AND URBAN AFFAIRS \n \n(SHRI HARDEEP SINGH PURI) \n \n(a)  to (c) : All houses in urban areas, including in Gu jarat, that did \nnot have access to toilet facilities, were prioriti sed to be provided \nwith individual household toilets or with Community  Toilets, as the \ncase may be.   \nContd..p.2 /- \n \n\n- 2 - \nUnder SBM-U, 4,371 Urban Local Bodies (ULBs) out of  the 4372 \nULBs in the country, have been declared as Open Def ecation Free \n(ODF).  \n \n4,316 out of 4372 ULBs have been ODF certified thro ugh third party \nverification process.  \n \n3,339 out of 4372 ULBs have been certified as ODF+.  An ODF+ city/ \nULB require all its Community and Public Toilets (C T/PTs) to be \noperated and maintained as per the protocol for ODF + rating, \nensuring their functionality and proper maintenance  for continued \nusage.  \n \n961 out of 4372 ULBs have been certified as ODF++. An ODF++ \ncity/ULB require it to address complete sanitation value chain, i.e., \nsafe containment, evacuation, transportation, proce ssing and \ndisposal of faecal sludge and septage from CT/PTs a nd ensuring \nthat no untreated sludge is discharged into open dr ains, water \nbodies or in open fields. \n \nThe State-wise details of the ULBs, including in Gu jarat, which are \ncertified as ODF, ODF+ and ODF++  is at Annex-I. \n(d): The physical progress made under the Swachh Bh arat Mission -\nUrban (SBM-U) since its inception on October 2, 2014 is at Annex-II. \n \n(e): No specific problem regarding construction of toilets in ULBs \nhas been brought to the notice of the Union Governm ent. As may be \nseen in Annex-II, the targets in construction of bo th Individual \nHousehold toilets (IHHLs) and CT/PTs under SBM-U ha ve been \nexceeded. \n \n***** \n \n  \n\nAnnex-I as referred in reply to para (a to c) of th e Lok Sabha Unstarred \nQuestion No.365 due for reply on 03.02.2022 regardi ng “Targets under Swachh \nBharat Mission – Urban”. \n \nName of State/UT No. of ULBs certified in the State / UT \nODF ODF+ ODF++ \nAndhra Pradesh 110  104  7 \nAndaman and Nicobar 1 1 1 \nArunachal Pradesh 23  0 0 \nAssam 96  27  0 \nBihar 131  24  0 \nChandigarh 1 1 1 \nChhattisgarh 168  168  169  \nDadra Nagar Haveli & Daman Diu  3  2 0 \nDelhi 5 4 3 \nGoa 14  14  0 \nGujarat 171  165  111  \nHaryana 81  66  14  \nHimachal Pradesh 61  26  2 \nJammu and Kashmir 80  18  0 \nJharkhand 42  41  3 \nKarnataka 272  152  2 \nKerala 93  31  0 \nLadakh UT 2 0 0 \nMadhya Pradesh 383  380  296  \nMaharashtra 391  388  213  \nManipur 27  3 0 \nMeghalaya 10  1 0 \nMizoram 23  0 0 \nNagaland 19  0 0 \nOdisha 114  91  21  \nPuducherry 5 3 0 \nPunjab 170  166  66  \nRajasthan 192  126  9 \nSikkim 7 3 0 \nTamil Nadu 666  500  0 \nTelangana 74  116  9 \nTripura 20  6 0 \nUttar Pradesh 666  644  31  \nUttarakhand 99  63  3 \nWest Bengal 96  5 0 \nTotal 4316  3339  961  \n \n  \n\nAnnex-II as referred in reply to part (d) of Lok Sa bha Unstarred Question \nNo.365 due for reply on 03.02.2022 regarding “Targe ts under Swachh \nBharat Mission – Urban”. \n \n(i). Toilet construction : \nType of Toilets Target Completed  Percentage \nProgress \nIndividual House \nHold Latrines (IHHL) \n58.99 Lakh Units 62.64 Lakh \n Units  (More than \n100%) \nCommunity/Public \nToilets  (CT/PT) \n5.08 Lakh Seats 6.21 Lakh Seats (More than \n100%) \n \n(ii). Open Defecation Free (ODF) status : \nODF certification type  Target No. of ULBs declared ODF \nODF All 4372 ULBs of \nthe Country \n4371 \nODF+ 3339 \nODF++ 961 \n \n(iii). Solid Waste Management :  \nThe Door to Door collection is being practiced in 9 7.01 per cent of the \nwards, i.e., in 86,454 out of the total 89,112 Wards.  \nSource Segregation is being  practiced in 87.58 per cent of the wards, i.e., \nin 77,961 out of the total 89,112 Wards.  \nAgainst 14 per cent in 2014, processing of municipa l solid waste is 71 per \ncent of the total waste generated per day, i.e., wa ste processed is \n1,02,104  Tonnes Per Day (TPD) out of total 1,43,80 8 TPD of waste \ngenerated. \n \n***** \n \n \n \n ",
    "ls|LS17_S8_U_366": "������������������� �\n����������������� �\n��������� �\n���������������������� ��� �\n������������ ���������� �\n�\n�������������������������� �\n�\n����� � ���������� �������������� �\n� �\n��������������������� ����� �\n�������������������� �\n�\n�� �� �������� ���� ����������� ���� ����������� ������� � ������� ������ ������ ���� �����\n���������������������� �\n�\n����� ��� ���� ���� �������� ������ ����� ���� ����������� ��� � �������� ��������� ��� ���� �����\n��������� ������ �\n�\n����� ����������������������������������������� ��������������������� �\n�\n����� ������������������������������������������������ ���������������������������������\n������������������ � ���� ��������� ������ �\n�\n����������� �\n�\n���������������� ��������� ��������������� ��������� �\n�\n����������������� �\n�\n���� ��� ��������� ������� ���� ����������� ��� ������ ��������� �������� ������ ������ ���������� �\n���� �������� ������������ ��� ��������� ����� ����� ���� ���������� ��� ���������� ����������\n���������� ����������������� ���� ������� ������ ��� �������� � ����������� ������������ ��� ����\n���������� ��������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n������ ��� ���� �������� ��� ������� ����� �������� ����� ������� ��� �������� ������ ������\n����������� ��������� ��� ��� ����������� ���� ����������� ����� ��������� ������������ ��� ����\n�������� ������� ������� ����������� ��� ����� ����� ���������� ������ ��������� ������ ���\n�������������� �������������� ������ ������� ������� ������� �������������� �����������\n����������� ��������� ���������� ���� ������ �������� ��������� ����� ������ ������� ����� �� �\n������������ ������������ ����������� ������� ������������ ������ ����� ���������� �������� ����\n������ ��� ���������� ������������ ��� ���� ������������ ������������� ���� ������ ������ �������\n����� ������ ����� ��������� ����� ���������� ���������������� ��� ��� ������ ������ ������ ����\n������� 