    "ls|LS17_S8_U_451": " \n \n�\n�\n������������������� �\n������������������� �\n�������������������������������� �\n��� ������ �\n���������������������� ����\n���������������������� ���������� ��������������� ���������������� �\n������������������������������\n�\n������������������������� ��������������������� ��\n���� �\n���������������������� �\n�\n����������������������������� ���������������������\n�\n���� �����������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n������������\n���� ��� ���� �������� ���� ����������� ���� ���� ����� ��� ����� ������ ����������� ��� ���� ���������\n��������������������������������������������������������\n���� ������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n���������������������������������������������������\n���� ����������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n��������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n��������������������������\n���� �������������������������������������������������������������\n�\n������ �\n���������������� �\n���������� � ������������� ��\n�\n�����������������������������������������������������������\n�������\n�\n� �\n� �\n\n \n \n���������� ��������� ��� ��� ������ ��� ����� ���� ��� � � �� ��� ���� ������\n������������������������� �������� ���������� ����������������� ��������\n���� ������������ ������ ��� ����� ������������ �������� ������ ��������\n���������������������������� �\n�\n�����������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n����������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n����������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n��������������������������������������\n�������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n���������� �������� �������������� �������������� �������������������������� ������ ������ ���������������� ������������������������������������\n�����������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n��������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n���� �������� ��������� ���� ��� ��������� ���� ��������� ������ ����������� �������������� ��������������\n������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n���������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n�������������������������������������������\n����\n�",
    "ls|LS17_S8_U_452": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA  \nMINISTRY OF SKILL DEVELOPMENT AND ENTREPRENEURSHIP  \n  \nLOK SABHA  \n  \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 452  \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 04.04.2022 \n \nAWARENESS ON SKILL DEVELOPMENT MISSION \n \n*452.   SHRI GIRISH CHANDRA: \n \nWill the Minister of SKILL DEVELOPMENT AND ENTREPRE NEURSHIP be \npleased to state: \n \n(a)  whether the Government is planning to bring in  any communication mechanism \nto be adopted at various levels to create awareness  about the need for skill \ndevelopment at local, State, district and village levels;  \n \n(b)  whether the Government is considering to adopt  State Skill Development Mission \nat State level to organise advertisements/campaigns  in local language through \nelectronic and print media;  \n \n(c)  the steps taken/being taken by the Government at school level to create \nawareness about vocational education, apprenticeship, etc.; and  \n \n(d)  whether the Government has entered into any pa rtnership with any of the \ninternational agencies for vocational training opportunities and if so, details thereof?  \n \n \nANSWER \n  \nMINISTER OF  \nSKILL DEVELOPMENT AND ENTREPRENEURSHIP  \n(SHRI DHARMENDRA PRADHAN) \n \n(a) to (d) A Statement is laid on the table of the House.  \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n  \n\nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (A) TO (D) OF LOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. *452 TO BE ANSWERED ON 04.04.2 022 ASKED BY \nSHRI GIRISH CHANDRA REGARDING AWARENESS ON SKILL DE VELOPMENT \nMISSION  \n \n(a) The Ministry of Skill Development and Entrepren eurship (MSDE) has undertaken \nvarious awareness campaigns, workshops, digital sem inars from time to time at  \nnational, regional, state, district and block level  with the support of more than 25000 \nplus  skill centers and institutes for promotion of  various skill development initiatives of \nthe Government. Besides, National Skill Development  Corporation (NSDC), Sector Skill \nCouncils (SSCs), State Governments, State Skill Development Missionsand District Skill \nCommittees also undertake awareness campaigns throu gh Public Information Bureau \n(PIB), and Print and Electronic media including soc ial media under the aegis of Skill \nIndia Mission. All these initiatives aim to make skills aspirational for youth. \n \n(b) Central Government in partnership with State Go vernments promotes skilling and \nentrepreneurship to develop the required training a nd skilling programs for youth. At \nStates level, States are encouraged to create State Skill Development Missions (SSDM) \nalong the lines of National Skill Development Missi on and duly supported by \nDistrictsCommittees at the functional tier.All implementation agencies are empowered to \nleverage wide network of media including the PIB, A ll India Radio, Doordarshanetc as \nwell as other media.  \n \n(c) The National Education Policy (NEP) 2020 envisa ges curriculum integration of \nessential subjects and skills in all schools and hi gher education institutions in a phased \nmanner to provide necessary vocational skills for v ariety of occupations along with \nawareness about the benefits of vocational education. \n \nThe Department of School Education and Literacy (Mi nistry of Education) is \nimplementing the scheme of Vocationalisation of Sch ool Education under the umbrella \nof ‘Samagra Shiksha - an integrated scheme for scho ol education’, a Centrally \nSponsored Scheme. The scheme aims at integrating Vo cational Education with general \nacademic education in all Secondary/Senior Secondar y schools; enhancing the \nEmployability and Entrepreneurial abilities of the students, providing exposure to work \nenvironment; and generating awareness amongst students about various career options \nso as to enable them to make a choice in accordance  with their aptitude, competence \nand aspirations. The scheme covers Government and G overnment aided schools. \nUnder the Scheme, 14,435 schools have been approved  across the country \nforintegrating vocational education in general education from class 9 \nth  to 12 th .  \n \nFurther, MSDE in co-ordination with Ministry of Edu cation (MoE) has launched the Skill \nHubs Initiative (SHI) as a pilot on 01.01.2022 unde r central component of PMKVY 3.0 \nwhich focuses on introduction of skill training programme in the education ecosystem as \nenvisioned in the National Education Policy, 2020 ( NEP, 2020). Skill Hubs are nodal \nskill centres identified to provide skill developme nt and vocational training opportunities \nto target population segments from class 6 \nth  to 8 th  (introduction to world-of-work through \norientation, industry visits, bag-less days), Class  9 th  to 12 th  (aimed at exposing students \nto skill development avenues), school dropouts, and  out-of-education (aimed for \nacademic credit, mainstreaming back to education an d or apprenticeship and \nemployment linkages).As on 23.03.2022, a total targ et of around 9.3 lakh students has \nbeen earmarked under SHI out of which, 1.56 lakh ca ndidates have been enrolled so \nfar. \n\n \n(d) The National Skill Development Corporation unde r the Ministry has signed \nMemorandum of Understanding (MOUs) with 8 countries  viz; Japan, UAE, Sweden, \nSaudi Arabia, Australia, Russia, Finland and Morocc o for cooperation in the field of \nvocational education and training. NSDC has partner ed with the Finnish National \nAgency for Education (EDUFI), Finland to promote an d facilitate the exchange of \nknowledge of new innovations and connect the provid ers within the vocational \neducation and training sector between the two countries. \n \n The Government of India and the Government of Japa n have signed a \nMemorandum of Cooperation (MoC) in January, 2021 on  a basic framework for \npartnership for proper operation of the system pert aining to “Specified Skilled Worker”. \nUnder this MoC, skilled Indian workers from fourtee n sectors viz; (1) Nursing care \n(Caregiving), (2) Building cleaning management, (3)  Machine parts & tooling industries, \n(4) Industrial machinery industry, (5) Electric, el ectronics and information industries, (6) \nConstruction industry, (7) Shipbuilding and ship ma chinery industry, (8) Automobile \nrepair and maintenance, (9) Aviation industry, (10)  Accommodation industry, (11) \nAgriculture, (12) Fishery & aquaculture, (13) Manuf acture of food and beverages, and \n(14) Foodservice industry have been identified for enhanced job opportunities for skilled \nIndian workers in Japan. \n \nFurther, MSDE and the Ministry of Justice, the Mini stry of Foreign Affairs, and the \nMinistry of Health, Labour and Welfare of Japan (Go vernment of Japan) have also \nsigned an MoC inviting candidates from India to Jap an under the Technical Intern \nTraining Program (TITP).It aims to transform India’ s skill ecosystem by sending and \naccepting technical interns from India to Japan, th ereby enabling Indian industries to \nimbibe the best practices of Japanese industries. \n \n***** \n \n \n ",
    "ls|LS17_S8_U_453": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF SKILL DEVELOPMENT AND ENTREPRENEURSHIP \n \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO .*453 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 04.04.2022 \n \nSKILL DEVELOPMENT SCHEMES IN KERALA \n \n*453. SHRI THOMAS CHAZHIKADAN: \n  \nWill the Minister of SKILL DEVELOPMENT AND ENTREPRE NEURSHIP \nbe pleased to state: \n \na) the details of the schemes currently being run b y the Government for Skill \nDevelopment of unemployed youth in urban areas in Kerala; \n \nb) the number of people who benefitted from these s chemes during the last \nthree years; and \n \nc) the number of people who secured jobs during the  said period? \n \n \n \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF  \nSKILL DEVELOPMENT AND ENTREPRENEURSHIP  \n(SHRI DHARMENDRA PRADHAN ) \n \n \n(a) to (c) :  A Statement is laid on the Table of t he House.  \n  \n\nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (A) TO (C) OF LOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. *453 TO BE ANSWERED ON 04.04.2 022 ASKED BY  \nSHRITHOMAS CHAZHIKADAN REGARDING SKILL DEVELOPMENT SCHEMES \nIN KERALA. \n(a) The Government is implementing various Skill De velopment \nSchemes/Programmes across Central Ministries/Depart ments, for providing a range \nof Skill Development training programmes on pan Ind ia basis. Under Skill India \nMission, the Ministry of Skill Development and Entr epreneurship is delivering skills \nthrough following skill development schemes across the country including Kerala: \nS.No. Schemes Objective \n1 Pradhan Mantri \nKaushal Vikas \nYojana (PMKVY) \nWith an aim to empower country’s youth and continue  \nthe journey of Skill India Mission in building Indi a as the \nskill capital of the world, the Ministry of Skill \nDevelopment and Entrepreneurship (MSDE) launched \nthe third phase of its flagship scheme—  Pradhan Ma ntri \nKaushal Vikas Yojana (PMKVY 3.0) in January 2021.  \n2 Jan Shikshan \nSansthan  (JSS ) \nScheme \nScheme of Jan ShikshanSansthan (NGOs) for Skill \nDevelopment to impart vocational skills in non-form al \nmode to non-literate, neo-literates, persons with \nrudimentary level of education upto 8 \nth  and school drop-\nouts upto 12 th  standard in the age group of 15-45 years. \nThe priority groups are women, SC, ST, minorities a nd \nother backward sections of the society. \n3 National \nApprenticeship \nPromotion \nScheme (NAPS ) \nThis Scheme is for promoting apprenticeship trainin g \nand increasing the engagement of apprentices by \nproviding financial support to industrial establish ments \nundertaking apprenticeship program under The \nApprentices Act, 1961 .   \n4 Industrial \nTraining \nInstitutes (ITIs )/ \nCraftsmen \nTraining Scheme \n(CTS ) \nThis scheme is for providing long \n-term training through \nIndustrial Training Institutes (ITIs ) operational across the \ncountry .The ITIs offer a range of vocational/skill training  \ncourses covering a large number of economic sectors  \nwith an objective of providing skilled workforce to  the \nindustry as well as self-employment of youth. \n \nOther Ministries running important skilling programmes in the urban areas: \nMinistry of Housing & Urban Affairs (MoHUA) is impl ementing a Centrally Sponsored \nScheme namely “Deendayal Antyodaya Yojana - Nationa l Urban Livelihoods Mission \n(DAYNULM)”, in the States/UTs including Kerala, to reduce poverty and vulnerability \nof urban poor households on a sustainable basis. Un der its Employment through \nSkill Training and Placement (EST&P) component, ski ll training is provided to the \nurban poor candidates in market-oriented certified courses for their placement in \nwage employment and self-employment opportunities. Ministry of Textiles is \nimplementing an umbrella skilling scheme viz. Samar th- Scheme for Capacity \n\nBuilding in Textile Sector (Samarth), signifying th e broad objective of the scheme to \nskill the youth for gainful and sustainable employm ent in the textile sector. Khadi & \nVillage Industries Commission (KVIC),through its De partmental and Non- \nDepartmental training centres and through other pro motional schemes, conducting \nSkill Development programmes in the country includi ng Kerala State for unemployed \nyouth to generate self-employment opportunities in traditional industries like \nbeekeeping, Pottery, leather, agarbatti making, soa p and detergent making,  Khadi \nspinning and weaving, baking and cake making etc. \n(b) The number of people trained under various skil l development schemes viz. \nPMKVY, JSS, NAPS and ITIs during last three years are attached at Annexure-I. \n(c) PMKVY  : The numbers of persons who secured jobs in Keral a during last \nthree years under schemeareas given below :    \n \nState \n2018-19 2019-20 2020-21 \nReported Placed Reported Placed Reported Placed \nKerala 6,501 8,263 1,213 \n \n \nAs per the Third-Party Evaluation Report on PMKVY 2 .0 (2016-20), it was found that \naverage monthly income of PMKVY trained and certifi ed individuals was 15% higher \nthan the comparison group. Moreover, 76% of the can didates acknowledged that \nafter the training, they have better chance of getting employment.  \n \nJSS:  The objective of training imparted under JSS is to  link the individuals for gainful \nlivelihood and supplement their family income throu gh self-employment and wage \nemployment. The providing of employment/placement t o the beneficiaries is not the \nmandate of the JSS Scheme. As far as the employment  of the JSS scheme \nbeneficiaries is concerned, third party evaluation report of the scheme has \nmentioned, “It is finally observed that as an impac t of the training programme \nconducted at JSSs, the self and wage employment and  private job have become \nevident”. The usefulness of the scheme would be fur ther self-evident from the fact \nthat same report has mentioned that 77.05% of the b eneficiary trainees have \nundergone occupational shifts.  \n \nCTS:  The final report of Tracer Study of ITI Graduates (published in January 2018 by \nthe Ministry of Skill Development & Entrepreneurshi p, GoI) mentions that 63.5% of \ntotal ITI pass-outs got employed (wage+ self, out of which 6.7% are self-employed).  \n \nNAPS:  Placements are not tracked in NAPS \n \n  \n\nANNEXURE-I \nAnnexure  referred to in reply to LSSQ No. *453 to be answered on 04.04.2022 \nregarding ‘‘SKILL DEVELOPMENT  SCHEMES IN KERALA” \n \nPMKVY: The number of persons trained during last three years:  \nState \n2018-19 2019-20 2020-21 \nTrained* Trained* Trained* \nKerala 35,973 78,523 31,077 \n*training figures inclusive of STT and RPL (non-placement linked component) of PMKVY scheme \n \nJSS: The number of beneficiaries trained during last 3 years:  \nState \nNumber of JSS beneficiaries trained  \n2018-19 2019-20 2020-21 \nKerala 6342 16247 13900 \n \nNAPS: The number of persons trained under NAPS during last 3 years: \nState \nNumber of persons trained  \n2018-19 2019-20 2020-21 \nKerala 3737 9858 6296 \n \nITIs:  Number of students enrolled in ITIs during last 3 years:  \nState \nNumber of persons trained  \n2018-19 2019-20 2020-21 \nKerala 38411 36004 31630 \n \n \n****** ",
    "ls|LS17_S8_U_454": "OIH \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF ENVIRONMENT, FOREST AND CLIMATE CHANGE \n \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 454 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 04.04.2022 \n \nFunds for Green India Mission \n \n454. DR. DHAL SINGH BISEN:  \n \nWill the Minister of ENVIRONMENT, FOREST AND CLIMATE CHANGE be pleased to \nstate: \n \n(a) the cost-wise details of the works carried out in Balaghat and Seoni district coming under \nBalaghat Parliamentary Constituency under the Green IndiaMission during the last three \nyears; \n(b) the details of the agencies or Non-Governmental Organisations (NGOs) through which the \nsaid workshave been carried out; \n(c) whether training equipments are provided to theunemployed youths under the said Mission; \nand \n(d) if so, the details of the unemployed people in Balaghat and Seoni district under Balaghat \nParliamentary Constituency who have been given training equipments under the said \nmission along with the cost of the training equipments? \n \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER FOR ENVIRONMENT, FOREST AND CLIMATE CHANGE  \n(SHRI BHUPENDER YADAV) \n \n(a) to (d): A Statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n \n*** \n \n  \n\nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARAS (a) TO (d) OF THE LOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 454 DUE FOR REPLY ON 04.04.2022 REGARDING ‘FUNDS \nFOR GREEN INDIA MISSION’ RAISED BY DR. DHAL SINGH BISEN, HON’BLE \nMEMBERS OF PARLIAMENT \n \n(a) & (b) The Madhya Pradesh State Forest Development Agency has carried out the GIM \nactivities which include advance&creation works, maintenance,distribution of \nalternate fuel energy devices and training programs with the financial implication of \nRs 651.00 Lakh during the last three years in Balaghat and Seoni Districts. The \ndetails of work carried out during last three years is placed in Annexure-1.The NGOs \nwere involved only in imparting trainings and their details are attached at Annexure-\nII. \n \n(c) &(d) The 12 training programs have been organized in the Balaghat and Seoni district under \nGIM. The total 302 individuals have been trained on various livelihood activities with \nthe financial implication of Rs. 18.10 Lakh. The details of the training programs are \nplaced in Annexure-III.List of the trained unemployed youth are compiled by the \nrespective division of the State. \n \n***\n\nAnnexure-I \n \nAnnexure referred to in reply to parts (a) & (b) of the Lok Sabha Starred Question No454 \ndue for reply on 04.04.2022 by Dr. Dhal Singh Bisen regarding “Funds for Green India \nMission” \n \nDetails of Work carried out under GIM in Balaghat and Seoni Districts during last three \nyears (2018-19 to 2020-21): \nS. No. Type of Work \nBalaghat Seoni \nPhysical Financial \n(Rs in Lakhs) Physical Financial \n(Rs in Lakhs) \n1. Advance Works \n(ha) 1480 240.30 510 81.67 \n2. Creation Works \n(ha) 1480 121.74 510 26.73 \n3. Maintenance \nWorks (ha) 790 148.20 269 0.61 \n4. \nAlternative fuel \nenergy devices \n(No.) \n175 \nSolar Cooker 10.50 \n175  \nPressure \nCooker \n3.15 \n5. \nNo. of Person given \ntrainings for \nlivelihood \n162 15.85 140 2.25 \nTotal - 536.59 - 114.41 \n \n***** \n\nAnnexure-II \nAnnexure referred to in reply to parts (b) of the Lok Sabha Starred Question No 454 due \nfor reply on 04.04.2022 by Dr. Dhal Singh Bisen regarding “Funds for Green India Mission” \n \nDetails of NGOs involved in training program in Balaghat and Seoni Districts under GIM \nS. No. Name of District Name of NGOs Type of Training \n1 Balaghat Asha Skill Development \nKhairi Balaghat, Dulanbai \nBauuddeshi Sansthan, \nBalaghat, CII Skill Centre, \nChhindwara, Rural Skill \nDevelopment Institution \nChhindwara \nBangle Making, Sewing, JCB \nOperator, Dairy Farming, Vermi-\ncompost Rope Making, Sewing, \nBeautician, Electrician \n2 Seoni Self-Employment Education \nSociety Seoni \nSecurity guard, Computer Skills, \nElectrician, Sewing, Embroidery, \nMacram Training \n \n***** \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \nAnnexure-III \nAnnexure referred to in reply to parts (d) of the Lok Sabha Starred Question No 454 due \nfor reply on 04.04.2022 by Dr. Dhal Singh Bisen regarding “Funds for Green India Mission” \n \nDetails of training given in Balaghat and Seoni and funds utilized for the same under GIM  \n \nName of \nDivision \nFinancial \nYear \nNumber of \nTrainings \nNumber \nof \nPersons  \nFinancial \nCosts \nRs. In \nlakhs \nNature of Trainings \nSouth \nBalaghat 2018-19 4 82 7.35 \nLac Bangle Making, Sewing \nTraining, JCB Operations, Dairy \nFarming and Vermicomposting \n2019-20 - - -  \n2020-21 4 80 8.50 \nWaste Cloth Rope Making, \nBasic Garment and Tailoring, \nBeauty Parlour and Hair Styling \nand Assistant Electrician Trade  \n SubTotal 8 162 15.85  \nSouth \nSeoni \n2018-19 - - -  \n2019-20 1 30 0.27 \nMulti-purpose Skill \nDevelopment for Security \nGuard, Computer Skill and \nElectrician \n2020-21 3 110 1.98 Sewing, Tailoiring and Macrum \nTraining \nSub Total 4 140 2.25  \nGrant Total 12 302 18.10  \n \n***** \n ",
